<Layout 
  title="General Relativity Cheat Sheet | Free Einstein, Geodesics, Black Holes"
  description="Complete general relativity cheat sheet with Einstein field equations, geodesics, and black holes. Free download for physics students."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>General Relativity<br><span>Cheat Sheet</span></h1>
    <p>Einstein field equations, geodesics, and black holes. From curvature to cosmology.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Einstein Field Equations</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Field Equations</h3>
        <pre><code>G_μν + Λg_μν = (8πG/c⁴)T_μν
G_μν: Einstein tensor (curvature)
Λ: cosmological constant
g_μν: metric tensor
T_μν: stress-energy tensor</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Physical Meaning</h3>
        <pre><code>"Spacetime tells matter how to move;
matter tells spacetime how to curve"
- John Archibald Wheeler</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Geodesics</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Geodesic Equation</h3>
        <pre><code>d²x^μ/dτ² + Γ^μ_αβ (dx^α/dτ)(dx^β/dτ) = 0
Γ^μ_αβ: Christoffel symbols
τ: proper time
Geodesics = "straight lines" in curved spacetime</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Schwarzschild Solution</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Schwarzschild Metric</h3>
        <pre><code>ds² = -(1 - r_s/r)c²dt² + (1 - r_s/r)⁻¹dr² + r²dΩ²
r_s = 2GM/c² (Schwarzschild radius)
Event horizon: r = r_s
Singularity: r = 0</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Applications</h3>
        <pre><code>Black holes: r < r_s
Gravitational time dilation
Gravitational redshift
Perihelion precession of Mercury
Light bending by gravity</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Gravitational Waves</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Properties</h3>
        <pre><code>Ripples in spacetime
Speed: c
Polarisation: + and × modes
Strain: h = ΔL/L
Energy flux: F = c³/(16πG)〈ḣ₊² + ḣ×²〉</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Download</h2>
    <p>Print this page or save as PDF for quick reference.</p>
    <p><strong>Tip:</strong> Use Ctrl+P (Cmd+P on Mac) to print or save as PDF.</p>
  </section>
</Layout>
